  "assessment": "Reviewed 13 direct interests, six stable directions, 22 topics, four examples and six outcome interests. Belief, traditions and public life generate the closest option, supported by Groningen’s historical, cultural, philosophical and social approaches. The public programme explicitly connects its academic identity to ethical questions in AI, genetics, climate and human life, supporting the second direction. Biblical languages and exegesis, and ministry or spiritual care, each identify a serious candidate but require sustained specialist formation. Examples and career trajectories do not establish course capabilities or professional qualification.",
